    "504A": {
      "title": "LONG TERM SHOULDER CLOSURE DETAIL",
      "note": "Referenced by Note 5 when movable barrier reopens the travel lane."
    }
  },
  "notes": {
    "confidence": "verbatim",
    "printed": [
      "1. LONG-TERM IS STATIONARY WORK THAT OCCUPIES A LOCATION MORE THAN 3 CONSECUTIVE DAYS.",
      "2. LEFT LANE CLOSURES ARE SYMMETRICAL TO RIGHT LANE CLOSURES. SUBSTITUTE LEFT LANE CLOSED SIGN (W20-5L), LANE ENDS SIGN (W4-2L), AND OBJECT MARKER (OM3-L).",
      "3. TEMPORARY / INTERIM PAVEMENT MARKINGS SHALL BE USED IN ACCORDANCE WITH THE CONTRACT DOCUMENTS. ANY EXISTING PAVEMENT MARKINGS THAT ARE CONFLICTING OR MISLEADING SHALL BE REMOVED OR COVERED.",
      "4. THE TEMPORARY POSITIVE BARRIER SHALL NOT BE PLACED ALONG THE MERGING TAPER. THE LANE SHALL BE CLOSED USING CHANNELIZING DEVICES AND PAVEMENT MARKINGS.",
      "5. IF WORK ACTIVITY PERMITS, A MOVABLE BARRIER MAY BE USED AND RELOCATED TO THE SHOULDER DURING NON WORK PERIODS OR AS PEAK PERIOD VEHICULAR TRAFFIC CONDITIONS EXIST. WHEN MOVABLE BARRIER IS USED, THE TEMPORARY WHITE PAVEMENT MARKINGS SHALL NOT BE USED. DURING THE PERIOD WHEN THE RIGHT LANE IS OPENED, THE SIGN LEGENDS AND CHANNELIZATION SHALL BE CHANGED TO INDICATE THAT ONLY THE SHOULDER IS CLOSED AS SHOWN ON THE LONG TERM SHOULDER CLOSURE DETAIL. IN ADDITION, THE ARROW PANEL SHALL BE PLACED AT THE END OF THE SHOULDER TAPER AND SHALL DISPLAY IN THE CAUTION MODE.",
      "6. UNLESS AUTHORIZED BY THE ENGINEER, THE MINIMUM LANE WIDTHS FOR WORK ZONE TRAVEL LANES SHALL BE AS FOLLOWS: FREEWAYS AND/OR EXPRESSWAYS IS 11'. THE MINIMUM LANE WIDTH FOR ALL OTHER TYPES OF ROADWAYS IS 10'.",
      "7. SEE NOTE 3 OF \"CHANNELIZNG DEVCES\" NOTES ON SHEET 619-010 FOR TEMPORARY POSITIVE BARRIER SUBSTITUTION"
    ],
    "planCallouts": [],
    "tableNotes": []
  },
